{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2 — Predicting interior temperature & humidity (multi-objective, multi-horizon)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal.** Given everything we know about the greenhouse *now*, predict **interior temperature** and **interior humidity** (centre sensor) at three lead times — **+1 h**, **+6 h**, **+12 h** — i.e. **6 quantities at once** (2 variables × 3 horizons): a *multi-objective* regression.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What the paper-level question is.** The value of each kind of *available information* — current observations, recent history, actuator data and day-ahead weather forecasts — and whether more complex models add anything **under comparable conditions**. The notebook is organised so that every comparison is made on the same rows, the same validation dates, the same selection criterion and the same refit rule.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Evaluation protocol (applies to every model in this notebook)**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Three-way chronological split with embargo** (`get_splits()` in `greenhouse_dataset.py`, shared with notebook 1): *inner train → 12 h embargo → validation → 12 h embargo → test*. The embargo equals the longest horizon, so no training target — inner or outer — ever falls inside the period that follows it.\n",
    "2. **Everything that is fitted is fitted on the training portion of the current stage only** — feature/target scalers *and* the cluster labels (notebook 1 saves `cluster_sel`, fit on the inner-train portion, and `cluster`, fit on the outer-train portion).\n",
    "3. **One common set of anchor hours.** A row is used only if it has a complete, gap-free 24 h history on the regular hourly clock (windows that would cross a data gap are discarded, not interpolated). Every model — single-timestep or sequence — trains and is scored on exactly the same anchor hours.\n",
    "4. **One selection criterion for every model family**: mean CVRMSE over the 6 targets, computed **in original units** (predictions and targets inverse-transformed), on the **same validation dates**. Tabular grids and the neural KerasTuner search both optimise this number.\n",
    "5. **One refit rule for every model family**: after selection, the winner is refit on the full outer-train portion (neural models for the number of epochs early stopping found on validation) and scored once on test.\n",
    "6. **Model choice is made on validation**; test is only used to report. The best model/feature set (2.8b) and the model used for the VPD analysis (2.13) are the validation-selected ones.\n",
    "7. **Neural models are reported as the mean ± std over 5 seeds**, and the main performance differences carry **paired temporal block-bootstrap 95 % confidence intervals** (2.8d, 2.9, 2.14).\n",
    "8. **Two baselines**: persistence (*\"in h hours it will be what it is now\"*) and **seasonal persistence** (*\"it will be what it was at the same hour yesterday\"*).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Feature ladder.** *no actuators → + current actuators → + actuator history → + cluster → + day-ahead forecast* (2.3), plus an explicit comparison of deployment information regimes (*snapshot / historical / NWP / oracle*, 2.14) where NWP and oracle use **matched weather variables**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Architectures** (no new ones added): Ridge / RandomForest / HistGB and LSTM / GRU / a compact attention block / MLP, each in a *t only* variant (current hour) and a *history* variant (a past window whose **length is itself selected on validation** from {3, 6, 12, 24} h; 2.7n reports the sensitivity to that length explicitly).\n",
    "\n",
    "Requires `pip install keras-tuner`. Set the environment variable `GH_SMOKE=1` before starting the kernel for a fast, reduced-budget dry run (few trials/epochs/seeds) — the numbers from a smoke run are **not** meaningful."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "6335ce05",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from IPython.display import display\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestRegressor, HistGradientBoostingRegressor\n",
    "from sklearn.multioutput import MultiOutputRegressor\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (mean_absolute_error, root_mean_squared_error, r2_score,\n",
    "                             precision_score, recall_score, f1_score,\n",
    "                             average_precision_score, confusion_matrix)\n",
    "\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "from tensorflow import keras\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras import layers\n",
    "import keras_tuner as kt\n",
    "\n",
    "from greenhouse_dataset import (\n",
    "    build_hourly_dataset, add_actuator_history, make_targets, TARGET_COLS,\n",
    "    ACTIVE_START, CONTINUOUS_COLS, ACTUATOR_COLS, EXTERIOR_COLS,\n",
    "    FORECAST_PREVDAY_FEATURE_COLS, make_forecast_horizon_features, get_splits,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.width\", 150)\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (11, 4)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- run budget ---------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "SMOKE = os.environ.get(\"GH_SMOKE\", \"0\") == \"1\"\n",
    "MAX_TRIALS = 2 if SMOKE else 20          # KerasTuner BayesianOptimization trials per (model, rung)\n",
    "MAX_EPOCHS = 3 if SMOKE else 100         # upper bound; early stopping on validation decides\n",
    "PATIENCE = 8\n",
    "SEEDS = (0, 1) if SMOKE else (0, 1, 2, 3, 4)   # final refits per neural model\n",
    "N_BOOT = 200 if SMOKE else 2000          # block-bootstrap replicates\n",
    "BOOT_BLOCK = 24                          # hours per bootstrap block\n",
    "RF_TREES = 20 if SMOKE else 200          # RandomForest size\n",
    "HGB_ITER = 30 if SMOKE else 300          # HistGB boosting iterations\n",
    "HORIZONS = (1, 6, 12)\n",
    "if SMOKE:\n",
    "    print(\"*** GH_SMOKE=1: reduced budget, numbers are NOT meaningful ***\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99ca84b8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.1 — Load, add actuator history, scope to the active period, attach clusters\n",
    "\n",
    "We build the hourly table, add the rolling actuator-history columns (`act_*_r3`, `act_*_r6`), then cut everything to the window where the climatic systems are actually operating. We also add the day-ahead forecast, aligned per horizon (`make_forecast_horizon_features`, see 2.3).\n",
    "\n",
    "Notebook 1 saves **two** cluster labels per hour: `cluster_sel` (scaler + K-Means fit on the inner-train portion only, used while selecting models on validation) and `cluster` (fit on the outer-train portion, used for the final refit scored on test). Both are one-hot encoded with the same column names (`clu_0` … `clu_{K-1}`); `df` carries the final labels and `df_sel` the selection labels. Nothing else differs between the two frames."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "cac63735",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "note: fc_temp_prevday still missing 364h after the short-gap fill; bridging with an unlimited forward-fill of its own past values (flagged in fc_temp_prevday_stale)\n",
      "note: fc_hum_prevday still missing 364h after the short-gap fill; bridging with an unlimited forward-fill of its own past values (flagged in fc_hum_prevday_stale)\n",
      "note: fc_viento_prevday still missing 260h after the short-gap fill; bridging with an unlimited forward-fill of its own past values (flagged in fc_viento_prevday_stale)\n",
      "added 26 actuator-history features, e.g. ['act_calefactores_r3', 'act_calefactores_r6', 'act_fog_r3', 'act_fog_r6']\n",
      "active-period span: 2026-04-24 00:00:00 -> 2026-07-13 22:00:00 | 1943 hours\n",
      "added 15 day-ahead forecast features, e.g. ['fc_temp_prevday_h1', 'fc_temp_prevday_h6', 'fc_temp_prevday_h12', 'fc_hum_prevday_h1']\n",
      "cluster dummies present in window (final labels): ['clu_0', 'clu_1', 'clu_2', 'clu_3', 'clu_4', 'clu_5', 'clu_6']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df = build_hourly_dataset(root=\".\")\n",
    "hist_cols = add_actuator_history(df, windows=(3, 6))     # act_*_r3, act_*_r6\n",
    "print(f\"added {len(hist_cols)} actuator-history features, e.g. {hist_cols[:4]}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df = df.loc[ACTIVE_START:].copy()                          # <-- re-scope\n",
    "print(\"active-period span:\", df.index.min(), \"->\", df.index.max(), \"|\", len(df), \"hours\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fc_hist_cols = make_forecast_horizon_features(df, horizons=HORIZONS)\n",
    "print(f\"added {len(fc_hist_cols)} day-ahead forecast features, e.g. {fc_hist_cols[:4]}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cluster labels from notebook 1 (final + selection-stage clustering).\n",
    "clusters_all = pd.read_csv(\"model data/clusters.csv\", index_col=0, parse_dates=True)\n",
    "assert {\"cluster\", \"cluster_sel\"} <= set(clusters_all.columns), \\\n",
    "    \"re-run notebook 1: clusters.csv must contain both `cluster` and `cluster_sel`\"\n",
    "K_CLUSTERS = int(clusters_all[[\"cluster\", \"cluster_sel\"]].max().max()) + 1\n",
    "cluster_cols = [f\"clu_{k}\" for k in range(K_CLUSTERS)]\n",
    "\n",
    "def cluster_dummies(labels):\n",
    "    d = pd.get_dummies(pd.Categorical(labels, categories=range(K_CLUSTERS)), prefix=\"clu\").astype(float)\n",
    "    d.index = labels.index\n",
    "    return d.reindex(df.index).fillna(0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_sel = df.copy()\n",
    "df[cluster_cols] = cluster_dummies(clusters_all[\"cluster\"])\n",
    "df_sel[cluster_cols] = cluster_dummies(clusters_all[\"cluster_sel\"])\n",
    "print(\"cluster dummies present in window (final labels):\", [c for c in cluster_cols if df[c].sum() > 0])"
   ]
  },
