    "targets = make_targets(df, temp_col=\"temp_centro\", hum_col=\"hum_centro\", horizons=HORIZONS)\n",
    "print(\"targets:\", TARGET_COLS)\n",
    "targets.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "61c512e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.3 — Feature sets: the ablation ladder\n",
    "\n",
    "Every rung adds one more group of information on top of the previous one, so the change in error isolates each group's contribution:\n",
    "\n",
    "| rung | contents |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **no actuators** | interior climate + exterior weather + time |\n",
    "| **+ actuators (current)** | above **+** this-hour on-minutes of each climatic system |\n",
    "| **+ actuator history** | above **+** rolling 3 h / 6 h running totals |\n",
    "| **+ cluster** | above **+** the regime label from notebook 1 |\n",
    "| **+ day-ahead forecast** | above **+** the `previous_day1` forecast value for the *target* hour t+h, one column per variable per horizon |\n",
    "\n",
    "The *climate* block already contains the interior temperature/humidity/pressure, so it is a strong base — the question is how much the **climatic-system** blocks add on top.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Only the `previous_day1` forecast is used.** The un-suffixed Open-Meteo columns (`fc_temp`, `fc_hum`, …) are the Previous-Runs API's \"latest available run\" for each timestamp — for a date in the past that is closer to an analysis than to a forecast issued with real lead time — so they are not fed to any model. The `*_previous_day1` columns were issued about a day before the target hour; since every horizon here is ≤ 12 h, the forecast for *t+h* was already available at *t*.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two further column groups are built here but used **only** in the information-regime comparison (2.14):\n",
    "\n",
    "* `oracle_hist_cols` — the **observed** future exterior weather at the target hour (`ext_temp`, `ext_hum`, `ext_rad_par`, `ext_viento`, shifted by *h*). Not deployable.\n",
    "* `NWP_MATCHED_COLS` / `ORACLE_MATCHED_COLS` — the forecast and the observed future weather restricted to the **same four physical quantities** (temperature, humidity, wind, radiation), so that the NWP-vs-oracle gap is not confounded by one side having precipitation and the other not (see 2.14 for the remaining radiation-unit caveat).\n",
    "\n",
    "Rows lacking any of these columns are dropped here, **before** the split, so every section shares one row set."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "ded5e4aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "added 12 oracle (observed future exterior weather) features, e.g. ['ext_temp_h1', 'ext_temp_h6', 'ext_temp_h12', 'ext_hum_h1']\n",
      "modelling rows: 1456 | candidate features: 98\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "time_feats = [\"hour_sin\", \"hour_cos\", \"doy_sin\", \"doy_cos\", \"hour\", \"month\"]\n",
    "climate = CONTINUOUS_COLS + EXTERIOR_COLS + time_feats   # un-suffixed FORECAST_FEATURE_COLS excluded, see 2.3\n",
    "\n",
    "feature_sets = {\n",
    "    \"no actuators\":           climate,\n",
    "    \"+ actuators (current)\":  climate + ACTUATOR_COLS,\n",
    "    \"+ actuator history\":     climate + ACTUATOR_COLS + hist_cols,\n",
    "    \"+ cluster\":              climate + ACTUATOR_COLS + hist_cols + cluster_cols,\n",
    "    \"+ day-ahead forecast\":   climate + ACTUATOR_COLS + hist_cols + cluster_cols + fc_hist_cols,\n",
    "}\n",
    "actuator_features = ACTUATOR_COLS + hist_cols     # everything \"climatic-system\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Observed future exterior weather at t+h -- ONLY for the non-deployable \"oracle\" regime (2.14).\n",
    "oracle_hist_cols = make_forecast_horizon_features(df, horizons=HORIZONS, source_cols=EXTERIOR_COLS)\n",
    "for c in oracle_hist_cols:\n",
    "    df_sel[c] = df[c]\n",
    "print(f\"added {len(oracle_hist_cols)} oracle (observed future exterior weather) features, e.g. {oracle_hist_cols[:4]}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Matched weather variables for the NWP-vs-oracle comparison (2.14): same four quantities on\n",
    "# both sides. Precipitation has no observed counterpart in the exterior station, so it is left\n",
    "# out of both. Radiation is global shortwave in the forecast and the PAR band at the\n",
    "# station -- same physical driver, different spectral band/unit (see 2.14 / 2.14a).\n",
    "MATCHED_PAIRS = [(\"fc_temp_prevday\", \"ext_temp\"), (\"fc_hum_prevday\", \"ext_hum\"),\n",
    "                 (\"fc_viento_prevday\", \"ext_viento\"), (\"fc_rad_prevday\", \"ext_rad_par\")]\n",
    "NWP_MATCHED_COLS = [f\"{f}_h{h}\" for f, _ in MATCHED_PAIRS for h in HORIZONS]\n",
    "ORACLE_MATCHED_COLS = [f\"{o}_h{h}\" for _, o in MATCHED_PAIRS for h in HORIZONS]\n",
    "assert set(NWP_MATCHED_COLS) <= set(fc_hist_cols) and set(ORACLE_MATCHED_COLS) <= set(oracle_hist_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "all_cols = climate + ACTUATOR_COLS + hist_cols + cluster_cols + fc_hist_cols + oracle_hist_cols\n",
    "required = climate + ACTUATOR_COLS + hist_cols + fc_hist_cols + oracle_hist_cols   # cluster dummies may be 0\n",
    "data = df[all_cols].join(targets).dropna(subset=required + TARGET_COLS)\n",
    "data_sel = df_sel.loc[data.index, all_cols].join(targets)     # identical except the cluster columns\n",
    "assert data_sel.drop(columns=cluster_cols).equals(data.drop(columns=cluster_cols))\n",
    "print(\"modelling rows:\", len(data), \"| candidate features:\", len(all_cols))"
   ]
  },
