   "source": [
    "## 2.5 — Metrics: **MAE**, **CVRMSE** (RMSE ÷ mean, as used elsewhere in the repo), and **R²**, per target.\n",
    "\n",
    "MAE is in native units (°C for `temp_*`, %RH for `hum_*`) and is **never averaged across the two variables**. Wherever one scalar is needed to rank or select models, the notebook uses the **mean CVRMSE over the 6 targets, in original units** (`mean_cvrmse`).\n",
    "\n",
    "`score_seeds()` scores a *list* of prediction frames (one per seed for the neural models, a single one for the deterministic tabular models and the baselines) and returns the mean and the standard deviation across seeds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "fd0b9ef6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def cvrmse(y_true, y_pred):\n",
    "    return root_mean_squared_error(y_true, y_pred) / np.mean(y_true)\n",
    "\n",
    "def score(y_true_df, y_pred_df):\n",
    "    y_pred_df = y_pred_df.loc[y_true_df.index]\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "        \"MAE\":    {c: mean_absolute_error(y_true_df[c], y_pred_df[c]) for c in TARGET_COLS},\n",
    "        \"CVRMSE\": {c: cvrmse(y_true_df[c], y_pred_df[c]) for c in TARGET_COLS},\n",
    "        \"R2\":     {c: r2_score(y_true_df[c], y_pred_df[c]) for c in TARGET_COLS},\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "def mean_cvrmse(y_true_df, y_pred_df):\n",
    "    \"\"\"THE selection criterion: mean CVRMSE over the 6 targets, original units.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return float(score(y_true_df, y_pred_df)[\"CVRMSE\"].mean())\n",
    "\n",
    "def score_seeds(y_true_df, preds):\n",
    "    \"\"\"preds: list of prediction DataFrames (one per seed). Returns (mean, std) score frames.\"\"\"\n",
    "    ss = [score(y_true_df, p) for p in preds]\n",
    "    stack = pd.concat(ss, keys=range(len(ss)))\n",
    "    return (stack.groupby(level=1).mean().loc[TARGET_COLS],\n",
    "            stack.groupby(level=1).std(ddof=0).loc[TARGET_COLS])\n",
    "\n",
    "TEMP_TARGET_COLS = [c for c in TARGET_COLS if c.startswith(\"temp_\")]\n",
    "HUM_TARGET_COLS = [c for c in TARGET_COLS if c.startswith(\"hum_\")]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aa018280",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.6 — Baselines: persistence and seasonal persistence\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Persistence** — *\"in h hours it will be what it is now\"*: the forecast for *t+h* is the value at *t*.\n",
    "* **Seasonal (daily) persistence** — *\"it will be what it was at the same hour yesterday\"*: the forecast for *t+h* is the value observed at *t+h−24*. Since every horizon is < 24 h, that value is already known at *t*.\n",
    "\n",
    "Persistence is hard to beat at +1 h; seasonal persistence is far stronger at +6/+12 h because the greenhouse climate is dominated by the daily cycle. Any claim of a forecasting gain should be read against **the better of the two**. `ref_baseline` picks, **per target and on validation**, whichever baseline has the lower MAE — test is not used for that choice either."
   ]
  },
