   "source": [
    "print(\"Parameter count (trainable weights, seed 0) per neural model x rung:\")\n",
    "display(pd.Series({k: v for k, v in GRID[\"n_params\"].items() if k[0] in NEURAL_MODELS})\n",
    "        .unstack().reindex(index=NEURAL_MODELS)[list(feature_sets)])\n",
    "\n",
    "def seed_table(seed_store, models, cols_keys, metric_fn):\n",
    "    rows = {}\n",
    "    for m in models:\n",
    "        row = {}\n",
    "        for fs in cols_keys:\n",
    "            if (m, fs) in seed_store:\n",
    "                vals = [metric_fn(s) for s in seed_store[(m, fs)]]\n",
    "                row[fs] = f\"{np.mean(vals):.3f} ± {np.std(vals):.3f}\"\n",
    "        rows[m] = row\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows).T\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"TEST mean CVRMSE, mean ± std across {len(SEEDS)} seeds:\")\n",
    "seed_table(results_seeds, NEURAL_MODELS, list(feature_sets), lambda s: s[\"CVRMSE\"].mean())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3445240b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.7n — How long a history window is useful? (lookback sensitivity)\n",
    "\n",
    "Review question: with ~1k training anchors, a 24 h window may make the recurrent/attention models sensitive to noise and spurious fluctuations, and the last few hours may carry most of the signal. The history variants in 2.7 already *select* `L ∈ {3, 6, 12, 24}` on validation; this section shows the **whole curve** for `L ∈ {1, 3, 6, 12, 24}` at the richest rung, keeping every other hyper-parameter fixed at its selected value:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **same anchors for every L** (all have a complete 24 h history, 2.4), so only the window length changes;\n",
    "* for each L: fit on inner train with early stopping on validation → validation score and epoch count → refit on outer train (neural: 5 seeds) → test score;\n",
    "* `L = 1` is the t-only input with the history model's hyper-parameters.\n",
    "\n",
    "RandomForest is left out only to bound runtime.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reading it.** A flat or rising curve beyond a few hours means the extra history adds little beyond what the engineered features (actuator rolling sums, time encodings) and the current observation already carry. A choice of L should be read off the **validation** column; the test column is for reporting."
   ]
  },
