   "source": [
    "print(\"VALIDATION -- mean CVRMSE across the 6 targets (original units): the SELECTION criterion\")\n",
    "val_ladder = pd.DataFrame({fs: {m: val_results[(m, fs)][\"CVRMSE\"].mean() for m in MODEL_ORDER}\n",
    "                           for fs in feature_sets})[list(feature_sets)]\n",
    "for name, b in baselines_val.items():\n",
    "    val_ladder.loc[name] = score(y_val, b)[\"CVRMSE\"].mean()\n",
    "display(val_ladder.round(4))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"TEST -- mean CVRMSE across targets (unitless):\")\n",
    "display(add_baselines(ladder_table(GRID, \"CVRMSE\"), \"CVRMSE\"))\n",
    "print(\"TEST -- mean R2 across targets:\")\n",
    "add_baselines(ladder_table(GRID, \"R2\"), \"R2\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "82d4e8d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.8b — The validation-selected model, reported on test\n",
    "\n",
    "`best_key` is the (model, feature set) with the lowest **validation** mean CVRMSE across the whole grid; test only reports it. It is compared, per target, with persistence, seasonal persistence and the reference baseline (the better of the two, chosen on validation). This is the model used in the rest of the notebook (ablations, importance, VPD)."
   ]
  },
