   "source": [
    "fs_best = \"+ day-ahead forecast\"\n",
    "mae_by_model = pd.DataFrame({m: results[(m, fs_best)][\"MAE\"] for m in MODEL_ORDER})\n",
    "mae_by_model[\"persistence\"] = baseline_scores[\"MAE\"]; mae_by_model[\"seasonal pers.\"] = seasonal_scores[\"MAE\"]\n",
    "print(f\"TEST MAE -- all models, '{fs_best}' (rows: target, columns: model)\")\n",
    "display(mae_by_model.round(3))\n",
    "print(\"seed std of MAE (neural models):\")\n",
    "display(pd.DataFrame({m: results_std[(m, fs_best)][\"MAE\"] for m in NEURAL_MODELS}).round(3))\n",
    "print(f\"TEST CVRMSE -- all models, '{fs_best}'\")\n",
    "display(pd.DataFrame({m: results[(m, fs_best)][\"CVRMSE\"] for m in MODEL_ORDER}).round(3))\n",
    "print(f\"TEST R2 -- all models, '{fs_best}'\")\n",
    "pd.DataFrame({m: results[(m, fs_best)][\"R2\"] for m in MODEL_ORDER}).round(3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "33ce4c9f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.8d — Paired temporal block-bootstrap confidence intervals\n",
    "\n",
    "For a comparison *A vs B* we take, per test hour and per target, the difference of absolute errors `|e_A| − |e_B|` (for neural models the absolute error is averaged over the seeds, so the mean of the differences equals the difference of seed-mean MAEs). The 95 % CI of its mean comes from a **circular block bootstrap** with 24 h blocks (`BOOT_BLOCK`), which keeps the within-day autocorrelation of forecast errors. Both models are evaluated on the same hours — the test anchors are contiguous — so the resampling is paired.\n",
    "\n",
    "`ΔMAE < 0` means **A is better**. With ~12 days of test data there are only ~12 independent blocks, so intervals are wide: a CI that includes 0 means \"not distinguishable on this test window\", not \"equal\".\n",
    "\n",
    "Comparisons (each \"best\" is chosen on **validation**, within the stated subset, at the richest rung):\n",
    "1. selected model vs reference baseline / seasonal persistence / persistence;\n",
    "2. best history model vs best t-only model (value of history);\n",
    "3. best neural model vs best tabular model (value of the more complex model families)."
   ]
  },
