  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5eb8b988",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Interpretation.** The cell below prints the reading **from this run's numbers** (importance shares from 2.9/2.12b and the ablation CIs above) instead of hard-coding it, so text and outputs cannot drift apart. (An earlier version of this text claimed a *double-digit* importance share; the outputs never supported that — read the share from the printed lines.)\n",
    "\n",
    "Physically, the effect of a vent opening or the fog running is already visible in the interior temperature/humidity/pressure sensors that every model reads, so for *forecasting* the actuator columns are largely redundant with the climate block, and with ~1k training anchors extra columns can add as much noise as signal. They matter more for a **control / what-if** model, where the actuators are the inputs being set (notebook 3)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "0c334167",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "* Actuator features: 9.5% of RF impurity importance -- single-digit share.\n",
      "* + actuator history vs no actuators (GRU): significantly better on ['temp_h1', 'hum_h1', 'temp_h6'], significantly worse on no target, not distinguishable on the rest.\n",
      "* + actuators (current) vs no actuators (GRU): significantly better on no target, significantly worse on no target, not distinguishable on the rest.\n",
      "* + day-ahead forecast vs + cluster (GRU): significantly better on ['temp_h1', 'hum_h1', 'temp_h6', 'hum_h6', 'temp_h12', 'hum_h12'], significantly worse on no target, not distinguishable on the rest.\n",
      "  (permutation shares per variable are printed in 2.12b)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def ci_summary(tab):\n",
    "    better = [c for c in TARGET_COLS if tab.loc[c, \"CI excludes 0\"] and tab.loc[c, \"dMAE (A-B)\"] < 0]\n",
    "    worse = [c for c in TARGET_COLS if tab.loc[c, \"CI excludes 0\"] and tab.loc[c, \"dMAE (A-B)\"] > 0]\n",
    "    return (f\"significantly better on {better or 'no target'}, significantly worse on {worse or 'no target'}, \"\n",
    "            f\"not distinguishable on the rest\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"* Actuator features: {act_share:.1%} of RF impurity importance -- \"\n",
    "      f\"{'single' if act_share < 0.10 else 'double'}-digit share.\")\n",
    "print(f\"* + actuator history vs no actuators ({m}): {ci_summary(abl_hist)}.\")\n",
    "print(f\"* + actuators (current) vs no actuators ({m}): {ci_summary(abl_current)}.\")\n",
    "print(f\"* + day-ahead forecast vs + cluster ({m}): {ci_summary(fc_ablation)}.\")\n",
    "print(\"  (permutation shares per variable are printed in 2.12b)\")"
   ]
  },
