   "source": [
    "## 2.12 — Feature importance, climatic systems highlighted"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "930fd50e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x800 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "top = imp.head(22).iloc[::-1]\n",
    "colors = [\"#d1495b\" if f in actuator_features else \"#5b8c9e\" for f in top.index]\n",
    "top.plot(kind=\"barh\", color=colors, figsize=(8, 8))\n",
    "plt.title(\"Random Forest impurity importance (top 22) — climatic systems in red\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"importance\"); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "98175481",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.12b — Permutation importance on test, per variable\n",
    "\n",
    "Permutation importance of the same `rf_imp` model on the test anchors: shuffle one feature, measure the increase in MAE. The earlier version used scikit-learn's multi-output `neg_mean_absolute_error`, which **averages temperature MAE (°C) and humidity MAE (%RH) into one number**. Here the score is computed **separately** for the three temperature targets (MAE in °C) and the three humidity targets (MAE in %RH), so each importance is in one physical unit. The actuator share is computed over the clipped-to-zero positive importances (permutation importances can be slightly negative from noise), so it is an approximation, not an exact analogue of the impurity share."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "96afda80",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[temperature] climatic-system features hold 7.1% of positive permutation importance (MAE increase in degC); impurity share for comparison: 9.5%\n",
      "act_pantalla_lat_sur_r3    0.0480\n",
      "act_pantalla_cenital_r6    0.0133\n",
      "act_pantalla_lat_sur_r6    0.0113\n",
      "act_pantalla_cenital_r3    0.0111\n",
      "act_vent_cen_este_r6       0.0088\n",
      "act_fog_r6                 0.0082 \n",
      "\n",
      "[humidity] climatic-system features hold 4.0% of positive permutation importance (MAE increase in %RH); impurity share for comparison: 9.5%\n",
      "act_fog_r6                 0.0388\n",
      "act_fog_r3                 0.0376\n",
      "act_pantalla_cenital_r6    0.0144\n",
      "act_pantalla_lat_sur       0.0127\n",
      "act_vent_lat_norte_r3      0.0124\n",
      "act_pantalla_cenital       0.0089 \n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.inspection import permutation_importance\n",
    "\n",
    "def group_mae_scorer(target_subset):\n",
    "    ix = [TARGET_COLS.index(c) for c in target_subset]\n",
    "    def scorer(est, X, y):\n",
    "        return -float(np.mean(np.abs(est.predict(X)[:, ix] - np.asarray(y)[:, ix])))\n",
    "    return scorer\n",
    "\n",
    "perm = {}\n",
    "for grp, tcols, unit in ((\"temperature\", TEMP_TARGET_COLS, \"degC\"), (\"humidity\", HUM_TARGET_COLS, \"%RH\")):\n",
    "    r = permutation_importance(rf_imp, test[imp_cols], y_test, scoring=group_mae_scorer(tcols),\n",
    "                               n_repeats=20, random_state=0, n_jobs=-1)\n",
    "    pi = pd.Series(r.importances_mean, index=imp_cols).sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    ps = pd.Series(r.importances_std, index=imp_cols)\n",
    "    share = pi[actuator_features].clip(lower=0).sum() / pi.clip(lower=0).sum()\n",
    "    perm[grp] = (pi, ps, share, unit)\n",
    "    print(f\"[{grp}] climatic-system features hold {share:.1%} of positive permutation importance \"\n",
    "          f\"(MAE increase in {unit}); impurity share for comparison: {act_share:.1%}\")\n",
    "    print(pi[actuator_features].sort_values(ascending=False).head(6).round(4).to_string(), \"\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "e7cbdf5e",
   "metadata": {},
