   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 8))\n",
    "for ax, (grp, (pi, ps, share, unit)) in zip(axes, perm.items()):\n",
    "    tp = pi.head(22).iloc[::-1]\n",
    "    ax.barh(tp.index, tp.values, xerr=ps.reindex(tp.index).values,\n",
    "            color=[\"#d1495b\" if f in actuator_features else \"#5b8c9e\" for f in tp.index])\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"Permutation importance, {grp} targets (actuators {share:.1%})\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(f\"increase in MAE when shuffled ({unit}, ± std over 20 repeats)\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c0312722",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.13 — Real vs. predicted Vapour Pressure Deficit (VPD)\n",
    "\n",
    "VPD is derived from temperature and humidity (Tetens), so this checks whether the two per-target errors of the **validation-selected** model compound or cancel in the quantity growers act on. For a neural model every metric is computed per seed and averaged. The two baselines are shown alongside."
   ]
  },
