   "source": [
    "vpd_best = sum(vpd_sources[\"model\"]) / len(vpd_sources[\"model\"])\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(len(horizons), 1, figsize=(12, 9), sharex=True)\n",
    "for ax, h in zip(axes, horizons):\n",
    "    ax.plot(test.index, vpd_real[h], label=\"real\", lw=1)\n",
    "    ax.plot(test.index, vpd_best[h], label=\"predicted\", lw=1, alpha=0.8)\n",
    "    ax.axhline(0.4, color=\"grey\", lw=0.6, ls=\"--\"); ax.axhline(1.6, color=\"grey\", lw=0.6, ls=\"--\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(f\"VPD +{h}h (kPa)\"); ax.legend(loc=\"upper right\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(f\"Real vs predicted VPD — {best_key[0]} ({best_key[1]}); dashed: provisional thresholds\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "04682920",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.13b — Critical-VPD event detection: hours **and** episodes, against the baselines\n",
    "\n",
    "Two separate extremes, per horizon:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **VPD too low** (`< VPD_LOW_KPA`) — excess humidity, disease/fungal risk;\n",
    "* **VPD too high** (`> VPD_HIGH_KPA`) — water stress / stomatal closure risk.\n",
    "\n",
    "> ⚠️ **Thresholds pending validation.** `VPD_LOW_KPA = 0.4` and `VPD_HIGH_KPA = 1.6` are provisional values from general greenhouse-VPD guidance and **must be validated with the agronomy expert** for this crop and stage before any conclusion is drawn. They are plain constants, independent of the split and never fit on data, so changing them only requires editing one cell.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hour-level** metrics treat each test hour as one sample (precision, recall, F1, false-alarm rate FP/(FP+TN), AUPRC with the continuous predicted VPD as score). Consecutive critical hours are *not* independent events, so **episode-level** metrics are added: an *episode* is a maximal run of consecutive hours (on the target-time clock) where the real VPD crosses the threshold.\n",
    "\n",
    "* `n_episodes` — number of real episodes (e.g. 25 low-VPD hours may be only a handful of episodes);\n",
    "* `episode recall` — share of real episodes with at least one alarm inside them;\n",
    "* `onset hit rate` — share of real episodes whose **first** hour was alarmed (i.e. caught *h* hours ahead of its start);\n",
    "* `alarm episodes` / `false alarm episodes` / `episode precision` — the same idea from the alarm side: runs of consecutive alarms, and how many of them overlap no real episode.\n",
    "\n",
    "Every metric is reported for the model **and** for persistence and seasonal persistence (same threshold rule on their forecasts), since an alarm that persistence would also raise has no forecasting value. For neural models metrics are averaged over seeds."
   ]
  },
