   "source": [
    "rows = {}\n",
    "for f, o in MATCHED_PAIRS:\n",
    "    for h in HORIZONS:\n",
    "        fc, ob = test[f\"{f}_h{h}\"], test[f\"{o}_h{h}\"]\n",
    "        row = {\"corr\": np.corrcoef(fc, ob)[0, 1]}\n",
    "        if f == \"fc_rad_prevday\":\n",
    "            a, b = np.polyfit(train[f\"{f}_h{h}\"], train[f\"{o}_h{h}\"], 1)\n",
    "            row[\"MAE (native units of observation)\"] = mean_absolute_error(ob, a * fc + b)\n",
    "            row[\"note\"] = f\"after linear map PAR ~ {a:.2f}*SW {b:+.1f} (fit on train)\"\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            row[\"MAE (native units of observation)\"] = mean_absolute_error(ob, fc)\n",
    "            row[\"note\"] = \"\"\n",
    "        rows[(o, h)] = row\n",
    "fc_err = pd.DataFrame(rows).T\n",
    "fc_err.index.names = [\"observed variable\", \"horizon (h)\"]\n",
    "fc_err.round(3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.14b — The regime comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "Rows = every architecture (plus the baselines); columns = regimes. Neural cells are mean ± std over the seeds. `NaN` marks combinations that do not exist by definition (history variants have no *snapshot* counterpart). Compare `historical` vs `snapshot` for the value of observing the past; `NWP (matched)` vs `historical` for the value of the forecast; `oracle (matched)` vs `NWP (matched)` for how much of the remaining error is associated with forecast error *on the same variables*."
   ]
  },
